    "band_performance": {
      "Jerry": "Rips scorching leads on Bertha and delivers a vibrant jam after Eyes of the World, though his guitar drifts sharp on Eyes and feels a bit overstimulated later in the set.",
      "Phil": "Provides a solid low‑end throughout and shines during the rare Hamstrung Blues duet with Brent, anchoring the rhythm section.",
      "Bob": "Brings high energy and stage presence; his rhythm work is lively but guitar slips on Eyes of the World and vocals on Estimated Prophet feel over‑theatrical, while he adds fun with a laugh during Sugar Magnolia.",
